## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1 — MQTT Broker**: Should we bundle **Aedes** (in-process broker, zero setup) or connect to an **external Mosquitto** broker? Aedes is much easier to run as a standalone demo.

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> **Q2 — MongoDB**: Make it **optional** (skip writes if not connected) so the simulator can run with console output only first?

> [!NOTE]
> **Q3 — Failure Injection**: Should failures inject **automatically** on a random timer (good for demo), or should we expose a **CLI command / REST endpoint** to manually trigger a specific failure mode (better for controlled testing)?

> [!NOTE]
> **Q4 — Tick Rate**: Default `2 seconds`. OK?

> [!NOTE]
> **Q5 — Simulation Speed**: Should the sim run in **real-time** or support a **time-acceleration factor** (e.g., 10× speed so bearing failure degrades in 10 min instead of 100 min)?

